# 2026-04-27 — Today I Learned (TIL)

TIL about the JS event loop: microtasks (Promise.then, queueMicrotask) run *after* the current stack but *before* macrotasks (setTimeout, setImmediate). Node has an extra priority: process.nextTick runs before Promise microtasks.

```js
console.log('start');

setTimeout(() => console.log('macrotask: setTimeout'), 0);

Promise.resolve().then(() => console.log('microtask: promise'));

queueMicrotask(() => console.log('microtask: queueMicrotask'));

if (typeof process !== 'undefined' && process.nextTick) {
  process.nextTick(() => console.log('nextTick: process.nextTick (Node only)'));
}

console.log('end');

/* Expected order in browser:
start
end
microtask: promise
microtask: queueMicrotask
macrotask: setTimeout

Expected order in Node:
start
end
nextTick: process.nextTick (Node only)
microtask: promise
microtask: queueMicrotask
macrotask: setTimeout
*/
```